mido: accept 16 KiB code-signing granularity on a 4 KiB-paged kernel

launchd never got past dyld:

  disallowing unsupported code signature page shift:14
  unable to create a validated cs_blob object: 85
  dylib cache "(null)" not loaded: code signature registration for shared cache failed
  shared_region: vm_shared_region_start_address() failed
  panic: initproc failed to start -- exit reason namespace 6 subcode 0x1
         Library not loaded: /usr/lib/libSystem.B.dylib

Root cause is not the root filesystem.  HFS+ mounts, dyld finds the shared
cache directory (/System/Library/Caches/com.apple.dyld/, hard-linked out of the
cryptex), opens the cache and asks the kernel to register its code signature.
The kernel refuses, and that single EBADEXEC unwinds everything above.

Why it refuses: every arm64 Apple binary is signed with a 16 KiB code-signing
granularity, i.e. CS_CodeDirectory.pageSize == 14 (the field is log2, so it is
a *shift*, and XNU prints it raw -- "shift:14").  cs_validate_codedirectory()
only accepts 12 or the kernel's own PAGE_SHIFT, and 0102/0103 pinned PAGE_SHIFT
to 12 because the Cortex-A53 in the SDM8953 implements no 16 KiB translation
granule (ID_AA64MMFR0_EL1.TGran16 == 0).  4 KiB pages are not a choice on this
SoC, so the 16 KiB signature has to be accepted instead.  Raising the reported
DRAM size (the stock ">1 GB => 16 KiB pages" rule) cannot work here for the same
reason: with TG0/TG1 = 0b10 there is no mapping at all, which is the silent
death 0102 describes.

Two changes, and both are needed:

  * cs_validate_codedirectory(): also accept PAGE_SHIFT_16K.  Without this the
    blob is never created, so no later step can help.

  * cs_validate_hash(): for a blob whose granularity is wider than PAGE_SIZE,
    report the subrange validated and consumed instead of hashing it.  This is
    not cosmetic: a fault hands that function exactly one 4 KiB page, so a
    16 KiB hash cannot be recomputed from it, and cs_validate_page() would call
    it again at a 4 KiB offset that is not a multiple of 16384 and take the
    "offset not aligned to cshash boundary" panic instead.  cs_validate_page()
    already has the matching case for exactly this shape (offset_in_page == 0
    and bytes_processed > PAGE_SIZE - FOURK_PAGE_SIZE sets VMP_CS_ALL_TRUE), so
    reporting one full granularity is what that caller expects.

XNU itself only supports the opposite direction (16 KiB kernel pages over a
4 KiB-signed blob, ubc_cs_convert_to_multilevel_hash(), guarded by
"PAGE_SHIFT <= csb_hash_pageshift -> nothing to do"): there is no path to
re-derive coarser hashes from finer pages.  Waiving the per-page hashes is the
only option short of re-signing the whole 2.6 GB shared cache, and this port
already requires launchd_unsecure_cache=1 to boot at all.

Everything else in the blob is still checked exactly as before: magic, hash
type and size, hashOffset/identOffset/scatter bounds, codeLimit, code slots and
the cdhash over the Code Directory, plus entitlements.  Only the page hashes of
16 KiB-signed blobs go unchecked.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c b/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
--- a/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/ubc_subr.c
@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@
 extern int cs_debug;
 
 #define PAGE_SHIFT_4K           (12)
+/* mido: iOS arm64 userland signs every 16 KiB (cd->pageSize is log2). */
+#define PAGE_SHIFT_16K          (14)
 
 static boolean_t
 cs_valid_range(
@@ -371,7 +373,24 @@
 	if (ntohl(cd->magic) != CSMAGIC_CODEDIRECTORY) {
 		return EBADEXEC;
 	}
-	if ((cd->pageSize != PAGE_SHIFT_4K) && (cd->pageSize != PAGE_SHIFT)) {
+	/*
+	 * mido: accept a code-signing granularity wider than the kernel page size.
+	 *
+	 * iOS arm64 userland is signed with 16 KiB hashes (pageSize == 14) while
+	 * this kernel runs 4 KiB pages: a Cortex-A53 implements no 16 KiB
+	 * translation granule, so PAGE_SHIFT is 12 and every Apple binary would be
+	 * rejected with EBADEXEC (85).  That is what kills launchd:
+	 *
+	 *   disallowing unsupported code signature page shift:14
+	 *   unable to create a validated cs_blob object: 85
+	 *
+	 * A single 4 KiB page cannot reproduce a 16 KiB hash, so cs_validate_hash()
+	 * waives the per-page comparison for such blobs instead of hashing the
+	 * wrong bytes.  The blob structure, the entitlements and the cdhash are
+	 * still validated here exactly like any other blob.
+	 */
+	if ((cd->pageSize != PAGE_SHIFT_4K) && (cd->pageSize != PAGE_SHIFT) &&
+	    (cd->pageSize != PAGE_SHIFT_16K)) {
 		printf("disallowing unsupported code signature page shift: %u\n", cd->pageSize);
 		return EBADEXEC;
 	}
@@ -5726,6 +5745,24 @@
 			if (hashtype->cs_digest_size > sizeof(actual_hash)) {
 				panic("hash size too large");
 			}
+			/*
+			 * mido: blob signed at a wider granularity than the kernel page
+			 * size (iOS arm64: 16 KiB hashes, 4 KiB kernel pages).
+			 *
+			 * cs_validate_range() and cs_validate_page() only ever hand us
+			 * PAGE_SIZE bytes, so the wider hash cannot be recomputed here --
+			 * and cs_validate_page() would otherwise fault a page at an offset
+			 * that is not a multiple of the blob granularity and panic on the
+			 * alignment check below.  Report the subrange as validated and
+			 * consumed (one blob-granularity step) so the fault path accepts
+			 * the mapping.  This port already boots with
+			 * launchd_unsecure_cache=1, i.e. an unsealed userland.
+			 */
+			if ((1U << blob->csb_hash_pageshift) > PAGE_SIZE) {
+				*bytes_processed = (1U << blob->csb_hash_pageshift);
+				*tainted = 0;
+				return TRUE;
+			}
 			if (offset & ((1U << blob->csb_hash_pageshift) - 1)) {
 				panic("offset not aligned to cshash boundary");
 			}
